			<div class="content" id="post-content-2336380">
									

<p>Both ideas are good, yeah. From a translation perspective, &quot;Holy Emperor&quot; could be a way to reference to &quot;Tennou&quot; in contrast to concepts relating to &quot;Teikoku&quot;, which are quite different things.</p>
<p>My personal idea was that the IJAMEA was created after the Meiji Restoration, and that it replaced/inherited mostly ad-hoc agencies that acted under the Tokugawa government, but there could very well have been a council since earlier times.<br />
And all of those things are possible at the same time, also; there was a council under the Emperor, and it lost most of its power with the court's decline and the rise of the Shogunate; and then it was revived in a way with the Meiji Restoration, and in parallel with that the IJAMEA is created.<br />
Or, you know, whatever fits everybody's particular headcanon.</p>

